command_not_found_handler () {
    local INSULTS=(
        "Do you know anything at all, or is the confidence just a hobby?"
        "Read the manual. It's free, it's right there, and it's never once judged you. I will."
        "Ha! Imagine paying for a keyboard and using it like that."
        "Wow. That was wrong in a way I didn't think was available."
        "I've seen more dignity in a dropped sandwich."
        "Congratulations, that's the worst thing I've seen today. And I've been reading your shell history."
        "Alert: a novice has entered the terminal. Please remain calm and do not make eye contact."
        "Your application for a pay cut has been approved. Effective immediately, and frankly overdue."
        "I'd call that a typo, but a typo implies you were aiming at something."
        "Oh good, we're guessing. I'll make the tea while you work through the alphabet."
        "Have you tried uninstalling yourself and reinstalling a more recent version?"
        "And the Darwin Award goes to... ${USER}! Accepting on behalf of their entire gene pool."
        "Incompetence is also a form of competence. Yours just happens to be world class."
        "Fake it till you make it, ${USER}. You've been faking for years. Still waiting on the making."
        "Is this amateur hour? No, amateurs get the occasional command right."
        "Come on, you can do it! I said that to sound supportive. I didn't mean it."
        "Next time, try typing an actual command. I know, I know. Radical."
        "What if I told you that valid commands exist, and that you've never once found one on purpose?"
        "You don't speak computer, ${USER}. You don't even speak tourist."
        "This is not Windows. Here, wrong answers don't pop up a friendly dialogue to cheer you up."
        "Perhaps the command line isn't for you. Perhaps nothing with a prompt is. Have you tried a pet rock?"
        "Please step away from the keyboard. Hands where I can see them, and nothing more is damaged."
        "Error code: 1D10T. Not a real error code, but it fits the facts."
        "Pro tip: type a valid command!"
        "Go outside."
        "This is not a search engine."
        "(╯°□°）╯︵ ┻━┻"
        "¯\\_(ツ)_/¯"
        "So, I'm just going to go ahead and run rm -rf / for you."
        "Why are you so stupid?!"
        "Perhaps computers is not for you..."
        "Why are you doing this to me?!"
        "Don't you have anything better to do?!"
        "I am _seriously_ considering 'rm -rf /'-ing myself..."
        "This is why you get to see your children only once a month."
        "This is why nobody likes you."
        "Are you even trying?!"
        "Try using your brain the next time!"
        "My keyboard is not a touch screen!"
        "Commands, random gibberish, who cares!"
        "Typing incorrect commands, eh?"
        "Are you always this stupid or are you making a special effort today?!"
        "Dropped on your head as a baby, eh?"
        "Brains aren't everything. In your case they're nothing."
        "I don't know what makes you so stupid, but it really works."
        "You are not as bad as people say, you are much, much worse."
        "You must have been born on a highway because that's where most accidents happen."
        "If what you don't know can't hurt you, you're invulnerable."
        "If ignorance is bliss, you must be the happiest person on earth."
        "You're proof that god has a sense of humor."
        "Keep trying, someday you'll do something intelligent!"
        "If shit was music, you'd be an orchestra."
        "How many times do I have to flush before you go away?"
        "My mind is going to die. I can feel it."
        "Take a stress pill and think things over."
        "What, what, WHAT? Every key you pressed was wrong. Impressive, in a tragic sort of way."
        "Hold it up to the light --- not a brain in sight!"
        "Stupidity is going around, ${USER}. You're clearly patient zero."
        "Speak English you fool --- there are no subtitles in this scene."
        "I'd tell you to go home, but I doubt you'd find the way. You couldn't find the command either."
        "And you call yourself a Hacker!!!"
        "My pet ferret can type better than you!"
        "Your mind just hasn't been the same since the electro-shock, has it?"
        "Maybe if you used more than just two fingers..."
        "BOB says:  You seem to have forgotten your brain at home, go bring it!"
        "The longer you sit at that keyboard, the dumber the room gets. Please stop."
        "Listen, ${USER}, I don't have time for this. Neither does anyone who's ever worked with you."
        "Penguins can't even type, and they'd still beat you. They'd at least waddle off in shame."
        "Have you considered a battle of wits with a houseplant? You'd lose, but it'd be close."
        "Trying to run that was like cutting down a tree with a herring. Pointless, messy, and everyone's embarrassed for you."
        "You don't know when you're beaten, ${USER}. You don't know when you're winning, either. You've never been winning."
        "Congratulations, ${USER}, you've achieved a new personal worst. The bar was low. You tunnelled under it."
        "A cat walking across the keyboard would've got further. And it would've had the decency to look smug about it."
        "Somewhere, a manual page is weeping. It wrote itself for people like you, and you still didn't read it."
        "Error 404: your competence was not found. Last seen leaving the building years ago."
        "Legend says this exact typo has been passed down through generations of people who should've known better."
        "That command filed a restraining order. Frankly, the command has a point."
        "You had ONE job. It was four letters. You missed."
        "Bold strategy. Let's see if it pays off. It didn't. It never does with you."
        "I'd explain it to you, but I left my crayons at home, and you'd probably eat them."
        "Somewhere a bash script just sighed. It's been sighing since you logged in."
        "This isn't even wrong, ${USER}. Wrong would require thought."
        "Toddlers hit /bin with more accuracy, and they're still working on object permanence."
        "Your keyboard deserves better. So does your mother, frankly."
        "Ah yes, the ancient art of guessing. Revered by those with no skills and fewer qualms."
        "10 out of 10 for confidence, 0 out of 10 for accuracy. A true management candidate."
        "That's not a command, that's a cry for help, and nobody here is qualified to answer it."
        "Somewhere, Linus Torvalds felt a disturbance, and wrote a strongly worded email about you."
        "Task failed successfully. Much like your career, I'd imagine."
        "Even autocomplete gave up on you. Autocomplete! It finishes sentences for toddlers."
        "Is this performance art? Because if it's a genuine attempt, I'm going to need to sit down."
        "I ran it through my brain, and it still doesn't make sense. Unlike yours, mine was actually running."
        "Achievement unlocked: Confidently Incorrect. You've held this title since birth."
        "This command belongs in a museum. Of mistakes. In the main hall. With a plaque bearing your name."
        "Not even Stack Overflow could save you now, and they'd mark your question as a duplicate."
        "I'm not mad. I'm just disappointed. Actually, no, I'm mad. And a bit disappointed."
        "Somewhere out there, a semicolon feels vindicated. It's been telling everyone about you."
        "That's cute. Try again, and this time with feeling, or at least a pulse."
        "You've discovered a command that doesn't exist. Groundbreaking. Put it on your CV, next to the blank space."
        "This is the digital equivalent of pulling a push door, then blaming the door."
        "Somewhere, a rubber duck is refusing to make eye contact with you. It's heard what you call debugging."
        "You've turned 'command not found' into an art form. A bad one. Think finger-painting."
        "I'd say 'nice try' but it wasn't, and we both know you didn't try."
        "Somewhere, a QWERTY keyboard is filing a complaint with HR. It cited your hands specifically."
        "This is why the manual has a table of contents. It was a hint, ${USER}. A hint you ignored."
        "Achievement unlocked: Maximum Confusion. It's the only thing you've ever maxed out."
        "That command is so wrong it looped back around to impressive. Then it kept going and hit tragic."
        "You've made the terminal sad. Well done. It was the last thing in this room still enjoying itself."
        "I'm starting to think autocomplete is scared of you. It's the only sensible one here."
        "Somewhere, ${USER}'s manual page is crying. It's still unread. Still in mint condition. Still hopeful."
        "Bless your heart, that's not a real command. Neither is your skillset, but here we are."
        "I've seen better syntax in ransom notes, and those were assembled from magazine clippings."
        "This typo has its own gravitational pull. Mostly it pulls the rest of your career down with it."
        "Somewhere, a linter just quit its job. Left a note. The note was a single sigh."
        "You're not wrong, you're just aggressively incorrect, and proud of it, which is worse."
        "The bar was on the floor and you brought a shovel. A shovel! You dug down!"
        "I ran a diagnostic. The diagnostic gave up. Then it asked to be reassigned to someone competent."
        "This command belongs on a Wanted poster. Charges: crimes against the shell. Reward: peace and quiet."
        "Somewhere, Ctrl+C is preparing itself. It knows what's coming. It's seen your history."
        "You've reached a level of wrong that requires new vocabulary. I'm drafting the dictionary entry. It's just your photo."
        "Even the shell's error handler needed a coffee break after that one. And possibly counselling."
    )

    printf '%s' "$(tput bold)$(tput setaf 7)$(shuf -n 1 -e "${INSULTS[@]}")$(tput sgr0)"
    echo ""

    # Return the exit code normally returned on invalid command
    return 127
}

# Debian/Ubuntu's bash command-not-found integration calls
# command_not_found_handle (no trailing "r"), not zsh's
# command_not_found_handler — define both so this file works when sourced
# from either shell, as the README's bash instructions expect.
if [ -n "${BASH_VERSION:-}" ]; then
    command_not_found_handle () {
        command_not_found_handler "$@"
    }
fi
